ertificate World Cinema Minor Academics Colleges and Schools Undergraduate Advising Summer Sessions Academic Resources Teaching and Learning Career Education Landman Library Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Online Programs Transfer International Direct Admissions Tuition and Financing Admitted Students Visit, Events, and Tours Home Life at Arcadia Get Involved Athletics and Recreation Arts at Arcadia Living and Commuting Belonging and Flourishing Campus Resources New Student Experience Because Arcadia Blog Study Abroad Preview the World First Year Second Year Semester or Summer Global Field Study Students from Another University About Arcadia Campus Map and Directions University Rankings Offices, Facilities, and Services Arcadia Advantage Leadership History Arcadia’s Systems of Support Community and Local Connections Healthy Knights Admitted Students Home / Admissions / Admitted Students Home / Arcadia University Admissions / Admitted Students Admitted Students Congratulations to all admitted undergraduate students ! Welcome to Arcadia University. It's time to celebrate, brag a bit, and take the next steps toward becoming a Knight. Submit Your Deposit Make it official and deposit today to become an Arcadia Knight!  If you are participating in FYSAE/SYSAE , you should submit both the Undergraduate Enrollment Deposit and the program-specific deposit. Undergraduate Enrollment Deposit Part-Time Undergraduate Deposit Gateway Deposit FYSAE Deposit SYSAE Deposit Raising Expectations for Academic Learning (REAL) Program Deposit Deposits are credited against your charges for the following semester. If you decline to enter the University by your acceptance date, your deposit will be retained and you will not be refunded. Already Deposited? Made your deposit and ready to join us this upcoming fall? Learn more about starting your new student journey as a Knight. Next Steps for New Students Next Steps for Financial Aid Check the mail for a red envelope containing your ﬁnancial aid award offer. Filing Deadlines For best chances of maximum aid, apply by the priority deadline of March 15 . Applications received after will be processed on a rolling basis. For Pennsylvania students , the FAFSA must be received at Federal Student Aid Programs by May 1 . Financial Aid Portal Check the status of your financial aid application in our Financial Aid Portal . To create an account, click “First Time User,” set your PIN, and log in using your Social Security Number as your Student ID. If you encounter an error, contact us with your name, address, and date of birth, and we’ll reset your PIN. Aid Offers Award offers are sent to all admitted students who submit the appropriate paperwork. You’ll be notified via email and can view, accept, or decline your aid in the Financial Aid Portal. Your award offer is not a bill; rather, it is a summary of the aid you’re qualified to receive for the upcoming year. Parents & Families The Arcadia Family Community will connect you with information about financial aid, campus life, academics, and more. Join the Community Admitted Grad Students You’ve been admitted to a master’s, doctorate or graduate certificate program, what comes next? Make Your Deposit Digital Downloads Show your Arcadia pride with these digital downloads! Download Now Community Learning Experiences Hands-on learning is part of the Arcadia experience, whether you’re a Biology or Theater Arts major. Our community learning experiences ensure you’re honing skills and exploring interests as early as your first year. Civic Scholars First-Year Study Abroad Experience Honors Program College2Career Gateway to Success Social Action and Justice Education (SAJE) Fellowship Admitted International Students Declaration of Finances Your Declaration of Finances will demonstrate that you have the funds to cover tuition and living expenses for one year (minus scholarships). Submit an official bank statement—within three months of the semester you applied for—that includes: The bank’s official name and seal; Your full legal name (or your sponsor’s); If you’re starting in the fall: Consecutive transactions from February, March, and April; If you’re starting in the spring: Consecutive transactions from September, October, and November; The official currency of the statement. If you have a sponsor, they must submit a Letter of Support that states: Their full legal name; Their relationship to you; The amount of support to be given; The duration of the financial support. You should plan to submit in early May to begin the review process as quickly as possible. For conditional admission , to determine the amount to show on your statement: One summer session ( six weeks ) ELI Tuition: $2,888 Campus housing: $2,000 ( optional ) Meal plan: $1,500 ( optional ) Textbooks: $180-$200 Student fees: $0 Arcadia health insurance: $160-$290 ( required if you don't have insurance ) Total: $6,878 One semester ( 15 weeks ) ELI Tuition: $5,775 Campus housing: $4,490-$5,300 ( optional ) Meal plan: $1,790 ( optional ) Textbooks: $180-$200 Student fees: $350 Arcadia health insurance: $320-$580 ( required if you don't have insurance ) Total: $13,975 Two semesters ( 30 weeks ) ELI Tuition: $11,550 Campus housing: $8,980-$10,600 ( optional ) Meal plan: $3,580 ( optional ) Textbooks: $360-$400 Student fees: $700 Arcadia health insurance: $640-$1,160 ( required if you don't have insurance ) Total: $27,950 Student Visa Students requiring an I-20 for the first time must present an I-20 or DS-2019 form—issued by Arcadia once your Declaration of Finances is reviewed and accepted—to the nearest U.S. embassy or consulate. You’ll receive your form via express mail, and must submit the I-20 mailing form to ensure timely delivery. You should apply for an F-1 or J-1 visa at the U.S. embassy or consulate. Call the office in your country to see what documentation is required for the application, and remember that you will need to schedule an interview as part of the process. Since many consular posts process applications by mail, you should allow plenty of time (the busiest months are June, July, and August). If you’re currently attending a U.S. school on an F-1 visa, transfer your I-20 record and submit a copy of your passport photo page, your F-1 visa, and your current I-20. Depositing Once your Declaration of Finances has been reviewed and approved, you’ll submit your deposit using one of the links above, by sending a U.S. check or money order, or by completing a wire transfer of funds . Let Enrollment Management know how you plan to deposit, and we’ll send you transaction requirements. Contact Us Enrollment Management 1-877-ARCADIA (1-877-272-2342) [email protected] Financial Aid 215-572-2980, 215-572-4049 (fax) [email protected] International Admissions +1-215-572-4049 (fax), AuInternational (Skype) (+1-877-272-2342 toll-free, +1-215-572-2910 direct) [email protected] Apply Visit Give Careers PortalGuard Apply Visit Give Careers PortalGuard 450 S. Easton Road Glenside, PA 19038 1-877-ARCADIA (1-877-272-2342) Campus Map & Tour EMERGENCY NEWS Student Resources Events & Calendar Offices & Facilities Athletics Canvas Self Service (staff login required) IT Help Desk INFO FOR Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Login Families Title IX All contents ©2026 Arcadia University. All rights reserved. Accessibility Non-Discrimination Notice Privacy Policy Close Search Form MENU A Prospective Student A Parent/Family Member A Current Student An Alumnus / Alumna A Faculty / Staff Apply Deposit Visit Give Request Information Majors and Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Accelerated Law Programs, BA to JD Accounting Major Acting Major Actuarial Science Major Agribusiness Minor AI in Education Online Certificate Applied Behavior Analysis Early Entry Master’s Program Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA), Online Graduate Certificate Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA), Online MEd Applied Health Sciences, BS – Online Degree Com