      "title": "Career Launchpad",
      "description": "Career Launchpad | Arcadia University Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav ARCADIA.EDU Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Handshake Personalize Your Alerts Meet with the OCE Explore Careers Special Interests Alumni BIPOC College2Career Scholars First Generation International Students LGBTQ+ Neurodiverse Student Employees Students with Disabilities Veterans Women By Community Art Business Communications Education Healthcare International Science & Tech Social Impact Still Exploring By Resource Connect with Alumni Explore & Plan Job & Internship Search Prepare & Apply Graduate & Professional School Work On-Campus Who You Are Students & Alumni Employers Faculty & Staff Career Influencers Parents & Families Prospective Students Career Outcomes Undergraduate Outcomes Graduate Outcomes Meet the OCE Meet Your Career Educators Meet Your Career Peer Mentors Meet Your Career Influencers Looking to hire Arcadia talent? Check out ways you can connect with Arcadia! 🚀 Welcome to the OCE Career Launchpad, where you’ll be able to: Read career news ; Discover who’s hiring ; Find jobs & internships ; Register for career events . Find your career communities from the “Explore Careers” & “Who You Are” menus above. Set up your preferences to receive email alerts with tailored career news and events that interest you! News & Articles ✨ Celebrating the Class of 2026 ✨ Share This: Share ✨ Celebrating the Class of 2026 ✨ on Facebook Share ✨ Celebrating the Class of 2026 ✨ on LinkedIn Share ✨ Celebrating the Class of 2026 ✨ on X Copy Link Thank you to everyone who stopped by the Office of Career Education table during Arcadia’s Senior Soirée: Toast to Commencement, celebrating the Class of 2026! 🎊 It was awesome connecting with so many graduating students as you get ready for life  … By Alice Song Show author info Alice Song Career Advisor Send Email Read more » The Secret to a Faster Job Search? Organization Share This: Share The Secret to a Faster Job Search? Organization on Facebook Share The Secret to a Faster Job Search? Organization on LinkedIn Share The Secret to a Faster Job Search? Organization on X Copy Link This article was originally published on Careershift . The difference between a slow job search and a fast one isn’t necessarily talent or connections. It isn’t luck. And it’s not even experience. It’s organization. You might already be qualified for the  … By Alice Song Show author info Alice Song Career Advisor Send Email Read more » Employer Spotlight: ChildCare Careers Share This: Share Employer Spotlight: ChildCare Careers on Facebook Share Employer Spotlight: ChildCare Careers on LinkedIn Share Employer Spotlight: ChildCare Careers on X Copy Link ChildCare Careers (CCC) is the largest staffing firm dedicated to the child care field. CCC provides fully qualified and pre-screened teachers, assistant teachers and site directors to child care centers, preschools, and before & after school programs. Since 1996, CCC  … By Alice Song Show author info Alice Song Career Advisor Send Email Read more » How to spot a fake job ad, and what to do if you’ve already applied Share This: Share How to spot a fake job ad, and what to do if you’ve already applied on Facebook Share How to spot a fake job ad, and what to do if you’ve already applied on LinkedIn Share How to spot a fake job ad, and what to do if you’ve already applied on X Copy Link This article was originally published on College Recruiter . You apply to a job. It seems like a good fit. Maybe even a great fit. Or even a too-good-to-be-true fit. The recruiter is impressed. Maybe even too impressed. They ask if  … By Alice Song Show author info Alice Song Career Advisor Send Email Read more » Employer Spotlight: Montgomery County Police – Maryland Share This: Share Employer Spotlight: Montgomery County Police – Maryland on Facebook Share Employer Spotlight: Montgomery County Police – Maryland on LinkedIn Share Employer Spotlight: Montgomery County Police – Maryland on X Copy Link The Montgomery County Department of Police is a nationally accredited agency and the primary law enforcement agency for Montgomery County, Maryland. With more than 1,300 sworn officers, assisted by over 700 support personnel, the agency provides the full spectrum of  … By Alice Song Show author info Alice Song Career Advisor Send Email Read more » View All Blogs Sidebar Quick Links Set Up My Career Consultation Research Career Paths & Majors Start My Career Action Plan Begin My Search Improve My Interviews Upcoming Events March Mar 02 Event: USPS Hiring Event Portsmouth NH -every Monday Mon, Mar 2 at 10am - Mon, Sep 28 at 4pm EST Monday, March 2nd at 10am - Monday, September 28th at 4pm EST April Apr 03 Event: USPS Hiring Event Portland ME every Friday Fri, Apr 3 at 10am - Fri, Sep 25 at 4pm EDT Friday, April 3rd at 10am - Friday, September 25th at 4pm EDT September Sep 01 Event: 2026-2027 Career Readiness and Mentorship Program Tue, Sep 1 at 8am - Mon, May 31 at 5pm EDT Tuesday, September 1st at 8am - Monday, May 31st at 5pm EDT Sep 08 Event: Kraft Heinz 101: Session 1 Tue, Sep 8 from 5pm - 6pm EDT Tuesday, September 8th from 5pm - 6pm EDT Sep 08 Event: TFA Philly Back to School Mixer Tue, Sep 8 from 5pm - 7pm EDT Tuesday, September 8th from 5pm - 7pm EDT View More Meet the Team Alison LaLond Wyant Executive Director, Civic & Global Engagement and Office of Career Education Meet Alison Dr. Cynthia Nichols Associate Dean for Advising & Experiential Learning Meet Dr. Cynthia Cheryl Lewis Associate Director for Student Employment Meet Cheryl Sonia Blount Associate Director for Employer Relations Meet Sonia Alice Song Career Advisor Meet Alice Kilolo Harmon Administrative Coordinator Meet Kilolo Undergraduate Student Outcomes All Years Class of 2025 Class of 2024 Class of 2023 Class of 2022 Class of 2021 Class of 2020 Class of 2019 Class All Academic Divisions/Schools All Programs/Majors Toggle charts The term Student Outcomes refers to undergraduate outcomes within the 6-9 months following graduation, providing a snapshot of Arcadia undergraduates’ success following degree completion. The data is collected through a survey distributed to students at graduation, and again in the months following, along with knowledge gained from faculty, LinkedIn, and phone calls to our graduates, in accordance with national standards. The knowledge rate of outcomes for each class was 73.3% for the class of 2025, 83.95% for the class of 2024, 79.8% for the class of 2023, 86% for the class of 2022, 79% for the class of 2021, 81% for the class of 2020, and 87% for the class of 2019, though response rates vary among colleges and departments. 01 First Destination 02 Top Employers 03 Job Titles 04 Top Locations of Graduates 05 Top Universities 06 Sampling of Graduate and Professional Schools Select data point First Destination Top Employers Job Titles Top Locations of Graduates Top Universities Sampling of Graduate and Professional Schools First Destination Top Employers Job Titles Top Locations of Graduates Arcadia graduates accept positions all over the globe. The graphic displays the proportions of graduates working across the United States. United States World Top Universities Sampling of Graduate and Professional Schools On average, nearly a third of Arcadia graduates enroll in a program of continuing education within 6 months post-graduation. The chart below displays the fields of study our graduates pursued. The represented \"other\" programs include degrees in International Peace & Conflict Resolution, Occupational Therapy, Applied Behavior Analysis, Medicine, Financial Mathematics, and many others. We don’t have enough student data to show you these results. Close Blog | Employers | Events | Jobs | Experiences | Resources | Outcomes | Team | Career Peer Advising | Contact 450 S. Easton Road, Glenside, PA 19038 1-877-ARCADIA ( 1-877-272-2342 ) 215-572-2900 My Arcadia Canvas Gmail Library Office of Student Accounts 